  "reasoning": "The claim that humans only use 10% of their brain is a well-documented and widely debunked myth. Modern neuroscience, utilizing neuroimaging technologies such as functional magnetic resonance imaging (fMRI) and positron emission tomography (PET), demonstrates that virtually all areas of the brain are active and have designated functions. Even during sleep or simple tasks, vast networks across the entire brain remain active, and there is no 90% portion that sits dormant or untapped. Furthermore, evolutionary biology and clinical neurology show that unused brain tissue naturally atrophies or degrades, meaning an unused 90% would not be maintained by the body.",
